From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@visma.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:50:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Translate keys with XkbLookupKeySym: XkbKeycodeToKeysym gives
 NoSymbol without XKB

On an X server without the XKB extension (kdrive's Xfbdev, TinyX) libX11's
XkbKeycodeToKeysym returns NoSymbol for every key, so Escape, the arrows and
Return did nothing; XkbLookupKeySym falls back to the core keymap there and
gives the same unshifted keysym where XKB exists.
---
 xmenu.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xmenu.c b/xmenu.c
index 1c879c4..9b3d189 100644
--- a/xmenu.c
+++ b/xmenu.c
@@ -2697,7 +2697,13 @@ xkeypress(Widget *widget, XEvent *xev)
 	if ((menu = widget->menus) == NULL)
 		return;
 	xevent = (XKeyEvent *)xev;
-	ksym = XkbKeycodeToKeysym(widget->display, xevent->keycode, 0, 0);
+	/*
+	 * XkbLookupKeySym rather than XkbKeycodeToKeysym: the latter
+	 * returns NoSymbol on a server without the XKB extension
+	 * (kdrive's Xfbdev), the former falls back to the core keymap.
+	 */
+	if (!XkbLookupKeySym(widget->display, xevent->keycode, 0, &(unsigned int){0}, &ksym))
+		ksym = NoSymbol;
 	if (ksym == XK_Tab && FLAG(xevent->state, ShiftMask))
 		ksym = XK_ISO_Left_Tab;
 	switch (ksym) {
